  <diagram name="LLMDraft: Schema vs Validators" id="llmdraftschema">
    <mxGraphModel grid="1" page="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1400" pageHeight="980" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="t1" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#ffffff;fontColor=#000000;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;fontSize=18;fontStyle=1;" value="LLMDraft: what reaches Azure OpenAI as a schema vs. what only Python ever checks" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="1320" x="40" y="10" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="t2" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#ffffff;fontColor=#666666;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;fontSize=11;" value="One Pydantic model, two different enforcement paths — see &#39;System Walkthrough&#39; sheet, /generate lane, steps 2-4 for where this sits." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="20" width="1320" x="40" y="40" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="src" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#666666;fontColor=#000000;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=10;fontSize=11;" value="LLMDraft(BaseModel) — ALL 7 fields below are LLM-authored, nothing skipped:&#xa;1. headline: str&#xa;2. subheadline: str | None&#xa;3. body_sections: list[BodySection] (2-3 items) — each with heading: str + text: str&#xa;4. call_to_action: str&#xa;5. sender_logo_caption: str&#xa;6. receiver_logo_caption: str&#xa;7. contextual_image_caption: str" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="140" width="560" x="420" y="70" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="leftHead" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontColor=#000000;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;" value="-&gt; becomes JSON Schema in response_format&#xa;SENT to Azure OpenAI — decoder-enforced live, during generation" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="50" width="480" x="100" y="400" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="leftBody" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontColor=#000000;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;fontSize=11;" value="- Field names + required/optional (str | None = optional)&lt;br&gt;- Data types: str, list[BodySection], nested object shape&lt;br&gt;- body_sections: Field(min_length=2, max_length=3)&lt;br&gt;  -&amp;gt; JSON Schema minItems=2 / maxItems=3&lt;br&gt;  (array LENGTH is schema-expressible, so IS enforced here —&lt;br&gt;   this is why the /generate diagram calls body_sections&#39;&lt;br&gt;   2-3 count &#39;structurally guaranteed&#39;, unlike word counts)&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div&gt;class LLMDraft(_HeadlineSubheadlineCtaLimits):&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; body_sections: list[BodySection] = Field(min_length=2, max_length=3)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; sender_logo_caption: str&amp;nbsp; # typically just the sender&#39;s display name&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; receiver_logo_caption: str&amp;nbsp; # typically just the receiver&#39;s display name&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; contextual_image_caption: str&amp;nbsp; # describes what the hero image should depict&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="220" width="480" x="100" y="460" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="rightHead" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;fontColor=#000000;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;" value="-&gt; stays as Python @field_validator code&#xa;NEVER sent to Azure OpenAI — the model never sees these rules" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="50" width="480" x="820" y="400" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="rightBody" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;fontColor=#000000;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;fontSize=11;" value="- headline &lt;=12 words, subheadline &lt;=20 words,&#xa;  call_to_action &lt;=25 words&#xa;- body_sections[].heading &lt;=12 words&#xa;- body_sections[].text &lt;=150 words&#xa;- word_count(v) = len(v.split()) — whitespace tokens,&#xa;  NOT model/LLM tokens&#xa;&#xa;WHY it can&#39;t travel: JSON Schema has no &#39;word count&#39;&#xa;keyword. maxLength counts characters, not words — this&#xa;rule literally cannot be expressed as a schema constraint,&#xa;for ANY Pydantic model, not just this one." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="220" width="480" x="820" y="460" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="parse" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontColor=#000000;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;fontSize=11;" value="client.beta.chat.completions.parse(response_format=LLMDraft)&#xa;SDK takes the model&#39;s raw JSON text and constructs&#xa;LLMDraft(**parsed_json) — ONE construction step.&#xa;EVERY validator above runs HERE: left-panel ones redundantly&#xa;(schema already blocked violations), right-panel ones for&#xa;the FIRST time — this is the only place they can run." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="120" width="500" x="450" y="710" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ok" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontColor=#000000;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;fontSize=11;" value="SUCCESS&#xa;valid LLMDraft object&#xa;returned to generate_draft()" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="90" width="350" x="250" y="850" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="fail" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;fontColor=#000000;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;fontSize=11;" value="FAILURE: pydantic.ValidationError&#xa;-&gt; fed back as feedback, retried&#xa;(System Walkthrough sheet, /generate lane, step 4)" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="90" width="350" x="780" y="850" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e1" edge="1" parent="1" source="src" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;fontSize=10;exitX=0.25;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="leftHead">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e2" edge="1" parent="1" source="src" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;fontSize=10;exitX=0.75;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="rightHead">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e3" edge="1" parent="1" source="leftBody" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;fontSize=10;exitX=0.7;exitY=1;entryX=0.2;entryY=0;" target="parse">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e4" edge="1" parent="1" source="rightBody" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;fontSize=10;exitX=0.3;exitY=1;entryX=0.8;entryY=0;" target="parse">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e5" edge="1" parent="1" source="parse" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;fontSize=10;" target="ok">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e6" edge="1" parent="1" source="parse" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;fontSize=10;dashed=1;" target="fail">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="notllm" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#999999;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=10;fontSize=11;dashed=1;" value="NOT in LLMDraft — added afterward, in generation.assemble_article(),&#xa;never written by the model:&#xa;- image_slots: list[ImageSlot] — built by resolve_image_slots() from the&#xa;  3 captions above + blob paths already on file (not authored directly)&#xa;- article_id, version — backend-generated (uuid4(), get_next_version())&#xa;- sender_id, receiver_id, theme — echoed from GenerateRequest (caller input,&#xa;  the model never even sees theme)&#xa;- total_word_count, created_at, status — computed/stamped in Python" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="150" width="560" x="420" y="225" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram name="ArticleOutput: Response Schema &amp; Assembly" id="articleoutputschema">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1815" dy="850" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1400" pageHeight="980" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="ao_t1" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#ffffff;fontColor=#000000;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;fontSize=18;fontStyle=1;" value="ArticleOutput: Response Schema — nothing here is typed by the LLM directly" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="1320" x="40" y="10" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ao_t2" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#ffffff;fontColor=#666666;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;fontSize=11;" value="Assembled in generation.assemble_article() by merging three sources below, then returned via routers/generate.py — see &#39;System Walkthrough&#39; sheet, /generate lane, steps 7-9." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="20" width="1320" x="40" y="40" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ao_src1" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontColor=#000000;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=10;fontSize=11;" value="Source 1: LLMDraft — LLM-authored&#xa;(see &#39;LLMDraft: Schema vs Validators&#39; sheet for full detail)&#xa;&#xa;headline -&gt; ArticleOutput.headline&#xa;subheadline -&gt; ArticleOutput.subheadline&#xa;body_sections -&gt; ArticleOutput.body_sections&#xa;call_to_action -&gt; ArticleOutput.call_to_action&#xa;sender_logo_caption, receiver_logo_caption,&#xa;contextual_image_caption -&gt; feed&#xa;resolve_image_slots() -&gt; ArticleOutput.&#xa;image_slots[].caption&#xa;(blob_path/image_url come from Table/Blob&#xa;Storage, NOT the LLM — System Walkthrough&#xa;sheet, /generate lane, steps 5-6)" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="240" width="420" x="40" y="80" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ao_badge1" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontColor=#9673a6;fontSize=9;fontStyle=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;dashed=0;" value="Ⓟ Pydantic model" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="16" width="100" x="40" y="60" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ao_src2" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#999999;fontColor=#000000;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=10;fontSize=11;" value="Source 2: GenerateRequest — caller input,&#xa;echoed straight through&#xa;&#xa;sender_id -&gt; ArticleOutput.sender_id&#xa;receiver_id -&gt; ArticleOutput.receiver_id&#xa;theme (ThemeColors: primary_color,&#xa;secondary_color, accent_color)&#xa;-&gt; ArticleOutput.theme&#xa;&#xa;The LLM never sees theme — it is not part&#xa;of the prompt or of LLMDraft&#39;s schema at all." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="240" width="420" x="490" y="80" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ao_badge2" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontColor=#9673a6;fontSize=9;fontStyle=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;dashed=0;" value="Ⓟ Pydantic body" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="16" width="100" x="490" y="60" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ao_src3" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;fontColor=#000000;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=10;fontSize=11;" value="Source 3: freshly computed backend values&#xa;(generation.py + storage.py, no LLM involved)&#xa;&#xa;article_id = uuid4()&#xa;version = storage.get_next_version(&#xa;    sender_id, receiver_id)&#xa;total_word_count = sum of word_count()&#xa;across headline + subheadline +&#xa;body_sections + call_to_action&#xa;(soft 300-600 target — logged, not enforced)&#xa;created_at = datetime.now(timezone.utc)&#xa;status = &quot;draft&quot;  (fixed Literal, no publish&#xa;workflow in this prototype)" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="240" width="420" x="940" y="80" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ao_merge" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontColor=#000000;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=8;fontSize=11;" value="generation.py: assemble_article(request, draft, image_slots) -&gt; ArticleOutput&#xa;called from routers/generate.py, right after resolve_image_slots() (System Walkthrough sheet, /generate lane, step 7)&#xa;ONE construction step — merges all three sources above into a single ArticleOutput object" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="70" width="760" x="320" y="360" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ao_e1" edge="1" parent="1" source="ao_src1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;fontSize=10;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.15;entryY=0;" target="ao_merge">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ao_e2" edge="1" parent="1" source="ao_src2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;fontSize=10;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="ao_merge">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ao_e3" edge="1" parent="1" source="ao_src3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;fontSize=10;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.85;entryY=0;" target="ao_merge">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ao_final" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#666666;fontColor=#000000;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=10;fontSize=11;" value="ArticleOutput(BaseModel) — response body of POST /generate (also returned by /revise)&#xa;field-for-field match of the layout/schema contract in docs/architecture/api-payload-schemas.drawio&#xa;&#xa;article_id: UUID                          image_slots: list[ImageSlot]  (exactly 3, Field(min_length=3, max_length=3))&#xa;sender_id: str                              theme: ThemeColors&#xa;receiver_id: str                           total_word_count: int&#xa;version: int                                 status: Literal[&quot;draft&quot;]&#xa;headline: str                               created_at: datetime&#xa;subheadline: str | None&#xa;body_sections: list[BodySection]  (2-3 items)&#xa;call_to_action: str" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="180" width="760" x="320" y="470" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ao_badgefinal" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontColor=#9673a6;fontSize=9;fontStyle=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;dashed=0;" value="Ⓟ Pydantic model" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="16" width="100" x="320" y="450" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ao_e4" edge="1" parent="1" source="ao_merge" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;fontSize=10;" target="ao_final" value="9. returns">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ao_note" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=10;fontSize=11;" value="Why the LLM cannot corrupt sender_id, version, or theme: structurally, it never sees those fields.&#xa;LLMDraft&#39;s schema (Source 1) has no sender_id / receiver_id / version / theme field at all — Azure OpenAI&#39;s&#xa;structured-output mode can only return values for fields it was given a schema slot for. Those fields are set&#xa;only in Sources 2 and 3, in plain Python, after client.beta.chat.completions.parse() has already returned.&#xa;There is no validation step &#39;catching&#39; a bad value here — it is not something the LLM could produce in the&#xa;first place. Same logic covers image_slots[].blob_path / image_url: Source 1 only supplies captions." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="120" width="1320" x="40" y="690" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
